### 🧩 DeepMind & Computability

Hassabis has articulated that:

* **Intelligence involves modeling patterns and systems that can be described as search over computable 
structures** (e.g., Turing machines or equivalent formal models). ([Reddit][1])

* The overarching goal of AI — and especially AGI — is to build systems that can **model and manipulate 
structured representations of reality in computational form**. ([Antoine Buteau][2])

A relevant sentiment emerging from his public discussions and those around his work is:

> *“Anything that can be modeled or predicted by a structured system can, in principle, be computed.”* ([Reddit][1])

This is consistent with Church–Turing computability (that any function that can be described algorithmically can be computed), and Hassabis’s framing that “intelligence is about efficient search and modeling” — a fundamentally computational project.

So although we don’t have a precise *textual* “everything is computable” moment from him in verified transcripts, 
the **intent and implications of his worldview** are that:

> **observable, representable phenomena — like structured intelligence, patterns in data, and bounded human 
experience — are amenable to computation.** ([Reddit][1])

